Right.  Uncontroversial, and IMO positive.  Particularly the 
"Harmonic Scoring" patch; Scores in the present Nethack game 
are essentially meaningless. 

> I've decreased prob of loading bones from 1/3 to 1/5, and increased
> prob of saving bones from 1-(1 / (1 + dlvl/4)) to 1-(1 / (1 + dlvl/
> 3)). My motivation for this change is that I wanted to see some older
> bones. I'm the only one who plays on this computer, and I got sick of
> only ever seeing the bones of my very recent characters. By reducing
> the loading prob, bones last a bit longer before they are discovered.
> I don't see this as an important change.

Actually, what you've done is to reduce very slightly the probability
of overwriting existing bones files when you die, while reducing
very significantly the probability of using them up next time you 
get there.  The visible gameplay change here is going to be mainly 
a reduction in encountering bones files.  Yes, the bones files you
get will on average be a few games older, but not by more than a 
few games. 

Given the stated goal, I think you'd prefer to check for the existence 
of a bones file for the current level, and then, if you find it, have 
a good chance of *not* overwriting it.  

That said? Reducing the probability of encountering bones files is 
probably good for gameplay.  

Nethack bones as they exist have a few fairly subtle dynamics that 
probably aren't planned.  For example if you play different classes 
all the time, your bones files will be on average 7 times as old by 
the time you get them. 


 
