This is a good direction to go in, and good for balance.  But it's 
a fairly serious thing to start messing with, and doing it in baby 
steps like this is probably the right thing. 
 
> I've reduced the protection bought from priests. Instead of turning
> probabilistic at +9 and maxing out at +20, it now turns probabilistic
> at +5 and maxes out at +14; however, the probability has been
> increased a bit. Also lowered initial range form 2-5 to 1-3. So
> typically this protection will now give around +5 or 6 instead of +9.

Probably a good thing, but characters can still get ridiculous 
armor classes by altar dancing.  Consider making protection from priests 
and protection from your God contribute to the same "divine protection"
armor class bonus and subject to a combined maximum. 
 
> I've changed the formula for the maximum level of random monsters from
> (clvl + dlvl)/2 to (clvl + turns/1000 +1 + 2*dlvl)/4.

This will require experimentation to get the right "turn factor";
Above you use 1000; It may turn out that a different constant is 
better.  I'd probably have dropped clvl out of the equation 
completely.  It makes a rapid dive into a considerably more 
viable strategy. 

> Finally, one last change, probably with the most significant change;
> and I'm a bit unsure about it. I've adjusted the probabilies
> associated with armour "mc" (magic negation, the code). Originally,
> the probability of a blockable magic attack succeeding was as follows:
> mc=0, p=100%
> mc=1, p=67%
> mc=2, p=35%
> mc=3, p+2%
 
> As I've said, I think the late game is a bit too easy. 
> So here's what I've changed it to:
 
> mc=0, p=100%
> mc=1, p=50%
> mc=2, p=25%
> mc=3, p=17%

From 2% to 17% is changing something core to many players' strategy 
by 750% in one stroke.  That's probably too drastic to do.  I would 
go as far as 5% (one attack in 20 rather than one in 50), let people
play it, and observe its effect on the game before going to 10%.  By
making this change alone (2% to 5%), you will MORE THAN DOUBLE the
difficulty of the late game. Changing from 2% to 17% all at once is 
more than I can interpret in terms of difficulty. 

